     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The projection code in <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">ctmm</span> received a large overhaul in version 0.5.0.<span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"> You can now reproject your data very easily, as demonstrated here: <a href=\"https://ctmm-initiative.github.io/ctmm/reference/projection.html#examples\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ctmm-initiative.github.io/ctmm/reference/projection.html%23examples&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457175389000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2NKFMQQu5v6WTbHAThE3D3\">https://ctmm-initiative.github.io/ctmm/reference/projection.html#examples</a><br></span></span></div><div><br><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"></span></span></div><div>Unfortunately a bug slipped into <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">as.telemetry()<span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">, when using the <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">projection</span> argument.</span></span> This bug is fixed in the development branch, which you can install via:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">devtools::install_github(&quot;ctmm-initiative/ctmm&quot;)<br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Apologies,</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Christen</span><br></span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
